  <static seed="144" source="Library/FortLewis/Calc3/12-1-Two-variable-functions/HGM4-12-1-28-Functions-of-two-variables.pg">
    <statement><p>(a) Describe the set of points whose distance from the z-axis
equals the distance from the xy-plane.</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p>A cylinder opening along the z-axis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A cone opening along the y-axis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A cylinder opening along the x-axis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A cylinder opening along the y-axis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A cone opening along the x-axis</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A cone opening along the z-axis</p>
</li>
</var></p>
<p>(b) Find the equation for the set of points whose distance from the z-axis
equals the distance from the xy-plane.</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>z^2 = x^2 + y^2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>y^2 = x^2 + z^2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>y^2 + z^2 = r^2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x^2 + y^2 = r^2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x^2 = y^2 + z^2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x^2 + z^2 = r^2</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
